    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Firestore Database**\n\nI've decided to use Google Cloud Firestore as the external document provider. My plan involves importing the necessary Google libraries in the Python script. It feels like a solid foundation, especially given its popularity.\n\n\n**Defining Query Logic**\n\nI'm now focusing on the core query function for `query_documents.py`. The plan is to define a function within the Python script to fetch documents from Firestore based on specified field values, using partition-style keys when applicable. This will streamline document retrieval for the user. I'll need to handle potential errors during the query execution as well.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789862222810,
          "start": 1789862220691
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc1a1393001KEdMS3tSeGqBgk",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc1a0f6d001wqzpLQqyKbNWI4",
