    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Considering NoSQL Options**\n\nI'm currently evaluating managed NoSQL providers for fetching documents. The goal is a Python script, `fetch_document.py`, to retrieve a document based on its ID. I need a concrete external choice and want to make the provider easily identifiable in the code, for instance with a constant or enum. This will streamline later refactoring if needed.\n\n\n**Implementing Firestore Integration**\n\nI've decided to proceed with Google Cloud Firestore for document retrieval in `fetch_document.py`. The code will now reflect this integration. My focus is on writing the core logic, which is using the `google.cloud.firestore` library. I'm ensuring there are clear provider-specific identifiers within the script, to allow straightforward swaps in the future. I'm about to start writing the core logic to connect and retrieve the document.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789862217896,
          "start": 1789862215931
